Camerapture, by chrrrs — https://github.com/chrrs/camerapture
Vendored from branch 26.2, commit 08eae6e (upstream version 1.10.15), MIT licensed; the
upstream licence sits beside this file in LICENSE and covers everything under this directory.

Photo Safari ships this code inside its own jar instead of depending on the Camerapture mod.
Registry, asset and data IDs are untouched (camerapture:camera, camerapture:picture and the
rest), so a world that used Camerapture keeps its photos, albums and picture frames. The flip
side is that the two cannot run together — photosafari declares "breaks": camerapture.

Changes made to the copy, all of them re-applied by ../import_camerapture.sh:
  - NeoForge sources dropped; this is a Fabric-only copy.
  - Tapestry (upstream's multi-loader layer) unhooked: its @FabricEntrypoint / @Implementation
    annotations are gone, entrypoints are declared in photosafari's fabric.mod.json instead,
    and Camerapture.PLATFORM / Camerapture.NETWORK name the Fabric implementations directly
    rather than looking them up as services.
  - Optional integrations dropped, since this mod does not carry their dependencies:
    Cloth Config (and with it Camerapture's own config screen and Mod Menu entry), Jade and
    First Person Model.
  - The Fabric client entrypoint and client mixins moved into the client source set, which
    this project keeps separate from main and upstream does not.

Photo Safari's own changes to Camerapture's behaviour are not made in here: they live in
photosafari's mixins (src/main/java/.../mixin, src/client/java/.../mixin/client), so this
directory stays a plain copy that can be re-imported.
